-- title:
--   The resolvent anchor point
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. Let $X$ be complete, $K$ nonempty, closed, convex and weakly compact, and $T$ nonexpansive on $K$.
--
--   1. **Resolvent anchor.** A chosen anchor point $x$ for the resolvent tail families $\{R_n\circ g:n\ge m,\ g\text{ generated}\}$. So
--   $$
--   x\in\overline{\mathrm{conv}}\,D_x ,
--   $$
--   and every point of $D_x$ is a weak limit of outputs $h(x)$ of maps from every tail. These are exactly the inputs needed for adaptive finite selection at the anchor.
